  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Emergent obligated $370M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Emergent received 177 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.1M, and obligations are up 2.0% year over year. Department of Defense is the single largest buyer with $102M obligated, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs with $70.6M and Department of State with $49.3M. Other buying agencies include Department of Homeland Security at $47.8M and Department of Health and Human Services at $28.9M. Other Computer Related Services is the dominant market for Emergent with $333M in obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing follows at $34.3M, with smaller amounts in Software Publishers and other computer-related NAICS categories. Fiscal-year obligations have varied: FY21 was $470M, FY22 was $518M, FY23 was $520M, FY24 was $396M, FY25 was $363M, and FY26 is $370M to date. Current-year totals are partial and represent contract obligations except where tables list total contract values for awards and expiring contracts. This summary focuses on obligations, award counts, buying agencies, and top markets to give a concise snapshot of Emergent’s federal business activity in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Emergent's largest federal buyers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $102M from Emergent, making the Department of Defense the largest buyer. Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70.6M and Department of State obligated $49.3M. Department of Homeland Security obligated $47.8M and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $28.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Emergent's federal obligations moved over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY21 obligations were $470M, FY22 obligations were $518M, and FY23 obligations were $520M. FY24 obligations were $396M, FY25 obligations were $363M, and FY26 obligations are $370M to date, which is up 2.0% year over year."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Emergent make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Emergent obligated $370M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Emergent received 177 awards in that period, with an average award size of $2.1M. Obligations are up 2.0% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Emergent?",
      "a": "Department of Defense obligated $102M, Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70.6M, and Department of State obligated $49.3M. Department of Homeland Security obligated $47.8M and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $28.9M. Other buying agencies include Department of the Treasury at $24.9M and Social Security Administration at $8.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Emergent sell to the government?",
